\ Two modules each define a same-shaped struct, so their generated `src>>`
\ accessors share one dispatch key and the table keeps only the later
\ registration. That collapse is benign because struct descriptors are
\ interned structurally: the surviving method's type guard compares
\ descriptors, which the two structs share. The image loader must restore
\ that interning, or the devirtualized accessor rejects the other module's
\ instances at runtime.

use { a-read: } "fixtures/struct_accessor_collision_a.1z" ;
use { b-read: } "fixtures/struct_accessor_collision_b.1z" ;

a-read print-line
b-read print-line
